From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:23:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] accel/tcg: cpu_exec_step_atomic runs in an RCU read-side
 critical section

cpu_exec holds rcu_read_lock() for everything a TB does; cpu_exec_step_atomic, which runs
one instruction's TB under start_exclusive() with the BQL dropped, did not. PANDA's callback
lists free unlinked entries after an RCU grace period (call_rcu), so a callback dispatched from
a TB run here must be inside a read-side critical section like any other. Also makes the
tb_lookup here (qht) follow the same rule as cpu_exec's.
---
 accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c b/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c
index 5482554b6..457ff29b4 100644
--- a/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c
+++ b/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c
@@ -587,6 +587,9 @@ void cpu_exec_step_atomic(CPUState *cpu)
     TranslationBlock *tb;
     int tb_exit;
 
+    /* As cpu_exec: what the TB runs (callbacks, lookups) may rely on RCU. */
+    RCU_READ_LOCK_GUARD();
+
     if (sigsetjmp(cpu->jmp_env, 0) == 0) {
         start_exclusive();
         g_assert(cpu == current_cpu);
-- 
